{"title":"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Convex_polygon\" title=\"Convex polygon\">convex</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral\" title=\"Quadrilateral\">quadrilateral</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96e470b7ce7a2f4d0c1ae064d2874ca377693897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2002$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> contains a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in its interior such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7d8d2226f3bad723a1a72d46b0acf7d64699be5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA = 24, PB = 32, PC = 28, PD = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"308\" height=\"16\" />. Find the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d743e4ed99802a3c4570b1e5f9c752fe35a4c7eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 4\\sqrt{2002} \\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ 2\\sqrt{8465} \\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"295\" height=\"21\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b40925f849c32fcd959193fc31fab1d1a98e4eaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(48+\\sqrt{2002}) \\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ 2\\sqrt{8633} \\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ 4(36 + \\sqrt{113})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"403\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/4/68414870d9584f78410cfea4874a58e80bd8a5ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ABCD] = 2002 \\le \\frac 12 (AC \\cdot BD)\\]\" width=\"248\" height=\"37\" />\n(This is true for any convex quadrilateral: split the quadrilateral along <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and then using the triangle area formula to evaluate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/a/63a0c06761ee664f3ab0910bbf3336158cbf1645.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ACB]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/1/fa16d5df87a703864688635578a8f358b31ad6ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ACD]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />), with equality only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39facf4ed73f7886f111ff2466878db18e5d8958.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC} \\perp \\overline{BD}$\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Triangle inequality\">triangle inequality</a>,  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/47354ad4fbf58262bd4a168ce26499d05b9aebb4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}AC &amp;\\le PA + PC = 52\\\\ BD &amp;\\le PB + PD = 77\\end{align*}\" width=\"177\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>with equality if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> respectively. Thus\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/763500d2bade003bb04e8fe0bcba8cc118de1a63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2002 \\le \\frac{1}{2} AC \\cdot BD \\le \\frac 12 \\cdot 52 \\cdot 77 = 2002\\]\" width=\"304\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Since we have the equality case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39facf4ed73f7886f111ff2466878db18e5d8958.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC} \\perp \\overline{BD}$\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, as shown below. \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be0cac31118507011fcd067dec64c89d4f9eee03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200); defaultpen(0.6); pair A = (0,0), B = (40,0), C = (25.6 * 52 / 24, 19.2 * 52 / 24), D = (40 - (40-25.6)*77/32,19.2*77/32), P = (25.6,19.2), Q = (25.6, 18.5); pair E=(A+P)/2, F=(B+P)/2, G=(C+P)/2, H=(D+P)/2; draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(A--P--B--P--C--P--D); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,A,WSW); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B,ESE); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,ESE); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,D,NW); label(&quot;\\(P\\)&quot;,Q,SSW); label(&quot;24&quot;,E,WNW); label(&quot;32&quot;,F,WSW); label(&quot;28&quot;,G,ESE); label(&quot;45&quot;,H,ENE); draw(rightanglemark(C,P,D,50)); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"275\" /></center>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>,  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/0/3a065c8fd0192f46aedd285c32c15ca942464e10.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} AB = \\sqrt{PA^2 + PB^2} &amp; = \\sqrt{24^2 + 32^2} = 40\\\\ BC = \\sqrt{PB^2 + PC^2} &amp; = \\sqrt{32^2 + 28^2} = 4\\sqrt{113}\\\\ CD = \\sqrt{PC^2 + PD^2} &amp; = \\sqrt{28^2 + 45^2} = 53\\\\ DA = \\sqrt{PD^2 + PA^2} &amp; = \\sqrt{45^2 + 24^2} = 51 \\end{align*}\" width=\"353\" height=\"108\" />\n</p><p>The perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/9822037ad21e4f2ece1212694d5b0fec0cca986d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB + BC + CD + DA = 4(36 + \\sqrt{113}) \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"366\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Draw the diagram out. Notice the very peculiar sets of numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/a/6daae1c2b26c5f0800682f8758a6327d3b5f5845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(24,32);(24,45);(28,45)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"194\" height=\"20\" />; these are simply multiples of the legs of well-known Pythagorean triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/9/dd96d4570025fb6e5cfe884ac452526ede0ad78f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,4,5);(8,15,17);(28,45,53)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"236\" height=\"20\" />, pointing to signs of possible right angles. We can assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1e40cf09c0391eb3a8cc22dfd9fbddcc03cd4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APB=\\angle BPC=\\angle CPD=\\angle DPA=90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"349\" height=\"15\" />, so the area of the entire figure would be:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/b/b1bb2304955211c464e9a48eae41ffa4b39c66a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot(24+28)(45+32)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot52\\cdot77=2002\\]\" width=\"368\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Thus this is the correct case, so finding the side lengths of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> by the Pythagorean Theorem yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/2/ff2913c8dfbf0acf66a31c49b621e09698af2bca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=40$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/1/501a20599354997d6de9100d7c92d24ca7a553c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=4\\sqrt{113}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"21\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/8/1783664734887198314dbf9789cdcfb945fcff48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=53$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/84242848f6d8d9b45d29678d75638ca8d9c6e78f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA=51$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, so the perimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93ef04313e2cdde7713e50cb4dc7f10b0d69b815.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40+4\\sqrt{130}+53+51=144+4\\sqrt{130}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }4(36+\\sqrt{113})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"475\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>~eevee9406\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B\">2002 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2002 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017200557\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.063 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 266/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7118/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.413      1 -total\n 54.05%    8.330      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 43.83%    6.755      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6316:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017200557 and revision id 255925. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}